id: 42
hanzi: 金属
pinyin: jīn shǔ
level: HSK 5
part_of_speech: Noun

meanings_summary:
  en: metal; metallic element; metallic material
  es: metal; elemento metálico; material metálico conductor y maleable

senses[1]{sense_number,part_of_speech,register,definition_en,definition_es,example_phrase}:
  1 | Noun | Standard | an opaque, lustrous chemical element or alloy that is a good conductor of electricity and heat, malleable, and ductile | elemento o aleación química brillante, opaca, dúctil, maleable y conductora del calor y la electricidad | 贵重金属 (precious metals)

example_sentences[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 古人常以“金石为开”来勉励后人，其中“金”指的便是坚硬无比的金属，象征着至诚之道能感通天地。 | Gǔrén cháng yǐ 'jīn shí wéi kāi' lái miǎnlì hòurén, qízhōng 'jīn' zhǐ de biànshì jiānyìng-wúbǐ de jīnshǔ, xiàngzhēng zhe zhìchéng zhī dào néng gǎntōng tiāndì. | Ancients used 'sincerity opens metal and stone' to inspire posterity; 'jin' denotes hard metal, symbolizing that absolute sincerity moves heaven and earth. | Los antiguos decían que la sinceridad abre el metal y la roca; el 'oro' representa el duro metal, simbolizando que el fervor sincero conmueve al cosmos.
  #2 | 在航空航天装备制造中，耐高温、耐腐蚀的新型特种金属合金是确保火箭发动机安全运行的关键材料。 | Zài hángtiān zhuāngbèi zhìzào zhōng, nài gāowēn, nài fǔshí de xīnxíng tèzhǒng jīnshǔ héjīn shì quèbǎo huǒjiàn fādòngjī ānquán yùnxíng de guānjiàn cáiliào. | In aerospace manufacturing, advanced specialty metal alloys resistant to heat and corrosion are critical materials ensuring rocket engine safety. | En la industria aeroespacial, las aleaciones metálicas avanzadas resistentes a altas temperaturas y a la corrosión garantizan el funcionamiento seguro del motor.

collocations[6]{hanzi,en}:
  贵重金属 | precious metals (gold, platinum)
  金属材料 | metallic materials
  重金属污染 | heavy metal pollution
  稀有金属 | rare metals; rare earths
  金属光泽 | metallic luster or sheen
  加工金属 | process or forge metal

idioms[4]{hanzi,pinyin,meaning_en}:
  精诚所至 | jīng chéng suǒ zhì | when utmost sincerity is attained, anything is possible
  金石为开 | jīn shí wéi kāi | even metal and stone open to absolute sincerity
  点石成金 | diǎn shí chéng jīn | touch stone and turn it into gold; turn ordinary into superb
  固若金汤 | gù ruò jīn tāng | as solid as a metal rampart and boiling moat; impregnable

character_decomposition[2]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,meaning_es,radical,radical_meaning_en,meaning_component,sound_component,stroke_count,composition_type,etymology_and_mnemonic,visual_mnemonic_story_en,visual_mnemonic_story_es,tone_mnemonic_anchor,cangjie,traditional}:
  金 | jīn | gold; metal; money; yellow | oro; metal; dinero; dorado | 金 | gold / metal | 土 (earth, mining ground) | 亼 (smelting roof / nuggets) | 8 | 单一结构 | Ancient bronze pictogram of gold and copper nuggets 丷 mined and smelted beneath an earthen shelter 土. | Precious mineral nuggets (丷) smelted from rich earthen mines (土) produce shining metal and gold (金). | Pepitas de mineral brillante (丷) fundidas de las entrañas de la tierra (土) alumbran el noble metal (金). | 55 | OPC | 
  属 | shǔ | category; belong to; genus; subordinates | categoría; pertenecer a; linaje | 尸 | corpse / body frame | 尸 (human lineage frame) | 蜀 (shǔ, caterpillar / Sichuan silk) | 12 | 半包围结构 | Simplified from 屬. Ancient pictogram of descendants connected by silk ribbons to family lineage 尸, denoting category or belonging. | Silk threads connect family members beneath one ancestral shelter (尸), grouping all who belong to the same genus (属). | Hebras de seda unen a los vástagos bajo el mismo alero (尸), reuniendo a cuantos pertenecen a un linaje o género (属). | 214 | SYTI | 屬

mnemonics_and_roots:
  composite_memory_hook_en: Precious mineral ores smelted from earth (金) grouped into their scientific family genus (属) constitute ductile metal (金属).
  composite_memory_hook_es: Brillantes minerales fundidos de la tierra (金) adscritos a su categoría química (属) integran la familia del metal (金属).
  cultural_and_cognitive_roots: In ancient China's Five Phases (五行), 金 represented the west, autumn, hardness, and justice. Paired with the classificatory morpheme 属 (category/genus), 金属 formed the modern scientific noun for all metallic elements.
  tone_sandhi_and_pitch_modulation: High level 1st tone followed by dipping 3rd tone: 'jīn shǔ' (55-214). Maintain a level high pitch on 'jīn' before letting 'shǔ' dip into low vocal register.

traps_and_cognates:
